    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the roster with an elite 83.53 score against Grant Holmes. While the optimizer factored in a 4% reduction for the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s projected output remains formidable thanks to a +16% boost from the SP\u2019s weak xERA and a +8% bump from his high-leverage spot in the lineup. Following closely are **Seiya Suzuki** (67.75) and **Gabriel Moreno** (67.70). **Seiya Suzuki** finds himself in a prime spot against Michael McGreevy, though managers must monitor the 37% rain risk, as weather could shorten his outing or dampen offensive production. **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Holmes, where his current form and lineup position are expected to carry the bulk of his production.\n\nTactical platoons and park factors are driving several secondary starts today. **Mickey Moniak** (66.21) remains a high-value play because of a massive +14% dynamic platoon boost against Logan Webb. Similarly, **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom** are leaning heavily on favorable park factors (+10%) to compensate for tougher matchups against the left-handed MacKenzie Gore. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** (64.79) is a key target for stolen base upside; with a slow pitcher delivery and a projected wind-out benefit (+5%), he remains a cornerstone for our pursuit of the scarce SB category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who sat just shy of the start threshold with a 54.31 score. While his speed profile usually makes him an auto-start, a -13% platoon penalty against Braydon Fisher ultimately tipped the scales in favor of more efficient bats. We are also monitoring the IL status of **James Wood** closely, as his absence continues to consolidate playing time for our core outfield. As all starters are currently listed under \"Lineup Pending,\" we are proceeding with these projections based on historical batting orders, but any late-scratches\u2014particularly involving **Seiya Suzuki** given the rain warning\u2014will require immediate pivots to our bench options like **Henry Bolte** or **Travis Bazzana**.",
